@startuml
title D-01 Management Dashboard Context Diagram
left to right direction

actor "Executive /\nManagement Viewer" as Exec
actor "Operations Manager" as Ops
actor "Finance /\nRevenue Assurance" as Finance
actor "Compliance Auditor" as Auditor
actor "Technical Operations /\nSupport" as Support
actor "Administrator" as Admin

rectangle "Management Dashboard\nand Reporting\n(read-only visibility,\nreporting, export, audit)" as MDR

rectangle "Central PMS\ncanonical control records" as CPMS
rectangle "Connector / Projection\nHealth Workflow" as Health
rectangle "Payment Orchestrator /\nPayments Domain" as Pay
rectangle "Site POS Server\nfiscal records/reports" as POS
rectangle "Operator Console /\nContinuity Workflow" as OC
rectangle "Vendor PMS / HCP\nnormal session authority" as Vendor
rectangle "Reconciliation Workflow" as Recon
rectangle "Audit / Evidence Workflow" as Audit

Exec --> MDR
Ops --> MDR
Finance --> MDR
Auditor --> MDR
Support --> MDR
Admin --> MDR

MDR --> CPMS : TariffSnapshot,\nPaymentAttempt,\nPaymentConfirmation,\nfiscal references,\nExitAuthorization status
MDR --> Health : connector status,\nlast poll,\nfreshness
MDR --> Pay : provider outcomes
MDR --> POS : authorized fiscal\nreferences/reports
MDR --> OC : governance and\ncontinuity review state
MDR --> Vendor : availability context\nthrough approved integrations
MDR --> Recon : reconciliation and\nsettlement status
MDR --> Audit : report access,\nevidence access logs

note bottom of MDR
Management Dashboard does not collect payment,
declare payment finality, issue Sales Invoices,
issue ExitAuthorization, open gates, approve discounts,
or mutate fiscal/payment records.
end note
@enduml
